government; the recent complex (often cataclysmic) events in Ukraine are investigated in the context of the everyday life of our contemporaries. How have Ukrainians pursued self-determination through culture and language after decades of oppression and control? The course is taught by a recent refugee from the Ukrainian war who is especially interested in Ukraine's new role on the world stage. Why the yellow-and-blue flags and bumper stickers in our streets and parking lots?", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Spring.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2867, "crseId": 371517, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "UKRAN", "catalogNbr": "3134", "titleShort": "Advanced Ukrainian II", "titleLong": "Advanced Ukrainian II", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "SEM", "ssrComponentLong": "Seminar", "section": "101", "classNbr": 6225, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "01:10PM", "timeEnd": "02:25PM", "startDt": "01/22/2024", "endDt": "05/07/2024", "instructors": [], "pattern": "MW", "facilityDescr": "Stimson Hall G12", "bldgDescr": "Stimson Hall", "facilityDescrshort": "STMG12", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "This course is part of the Shared Course Initiative (SCI) and will be taught from Columbia University using videoconferencing technology. Meetings will occur in one of Cornell\u2019s distance-education classrooms at Stimson Hall. Questions relating to placement, scheduling or the SCI may be directed to Ahmed Shamim, as3969@cornell.edu."}], "